the surrounding system, including repo context, tool design, prompt-cache s=
tability, memory, and long-session continuity.</p><p>That distinction matte=
rs because when we talk about the coding capabilities of LLMs, people often=
 collapse the model, the reasoning behavior, and the agent product into one=
 thing. But before getting into the coding agent specifics, let me briefly =
provide a bit more context on the difference between the broader concepts, =
the LLMs, reasoning models, and agents.</p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post"=
><strong>On The Relationship Between LLMs, Reasoning Models, and Agents</st=
rong><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-positio=
